{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Josh Groban feels like a natural next choice after Stages because I want more of his expressive singing and orchestral sound.",
    "Partners fits my interest in polished vocal performances, while the duet format offers an appealing connection to my crossover listening."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "PTX, Vol. 1 emphasizes contemporary a cappella, whereas I currently want orchestral accompaniment and familiar melodies; vocal harmonies alone are not enough.",
    "Hamilton connects loosely with my interest in theatrical singing, but its rhythm-driven approach does not match the flowing vocal performances I want now."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My Christmas listening seems to have been treated as an ongoing desire for holiday albums, although I would choose something nonseasonal today.",
    "My interest in singing seems to have been stretched across very different styles, even though accompaniment and delivery strongly affect what I choose."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My listening to Stages, Under One Sky, and Amor & Pasion makes expressive crossover vocals a stronger draw today than a broad connection to popular singing.",
    "I can enjoy country melodies, songwriting, and holiday harmonies without wanting them immediately; today my priority is orchestral vocal music, and I would need to know the performers before choosing an album called Duets."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my interest in melodic singing but give too little weight to my current preference for expressive, orchestral crossover vocals."
}"}
